-- title:
--   Symmetry of the maximum-norm distance
-- statement:
--   For all $x,y \in \mathbb{R}^d$,
--   $$\|x-y\|_\infty \;=\; \|y-x\|_\infty,
--   \qquad\text{where}\quad \|x\|_\infty = \sup_i |x_i| .$$
--
--   The maximum norm induces a genuine metric, and this is its symmetry. It is used constantly when a condition such as "$y$ lies in the cube of side $h$ about $x$" has to be read with the roles of the two points exchanged.
